Rewrite the given Python code to calculate the factorial of a number using recursion and memoization.

def recursive_factorial(n, memo={}):
    if n == 0:
        return 1
    elif n in memo:
        return memo[n]
    else:
        memo[n] = n * recursive_factorial(n-1)
        return memo[n]

In this rewritten test, we have introduced memoization to optimize the recursive calculation of the factorial. The memo dictionary is used to store previously computed factorial values, allowing us to avoid redundant calculations. This approach improves the efficiency of the recursive solution and reduces the time complexity.

